2.1. The Contractor shall provide the following cleaning and housekeeping services at the Premises:

(a) Daily cleaning of all common areas including lobbies, corridors, staircases, lifts, and entrance areas;
(b) Cleaning and mopping of all lobby floors, staircase floors, and common passage areas using appropriate cleaning agents and equipment;
(c) Cleaning of all glass surfaces, including entrance doors, lobby glass partitions, and lift cabin interiors;
(d) Dusting and wiping of all handrails, grills, switchboards, and other fixtures in common areas;
(e) Cleaning of all service areas including pump rooms, electrical rooms, and DG set room floors;
(f) Daily removal and disposal of garbage from all floors and garbage chute rooms to the designated municipal collection point;
(g) Cleaning and maintenance of the clubhouse, including the gymnasium, multipurpose hall, and common washrooms;
(h) Weekly deep cleaning of the swimming pool deck area and surrounding tiles;
(i) Pest control coordination as per the schedule specified in Annexure B (to be arranged by the Society through a separate pest control vendor; the Contractor shall only provide access facilitation and post-treatment cleaning);
(j) Any other cleaning work as may be reasonably directed by the Managing Committee from time to time, provided such work falls within the general scope of cleaning and housekeeping services.

2.2. The Contractor shall deploy a minimum of the following personnel on the Premises:

| Sr. No. | Category of Personnel | Minimum Number | Working Hours |
|---------|----------------------|----------------|---------------|
| 1 | Supervisor | 1 | 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM, all days |
| 2 | General Cleaners | 8 | 7:00 AM to 3:00 PM (4 cleaners) and 2:00 PM to 10:00 PM (4 cleaners) |
| 3 | Garbage Collection Staff | 2 | 6:00 AM to 10:00 AM and 4:00 PM to 8:00 PM |
| 4 | Clubhouse Attendant | 1 | 10:00 AM to 8:00 PM, all days |

2.3. The Contractor shall ensure that all deployed personnel are:
(a) Above 18 years of age;
(b) Physically fit for the duties assigned;
(c) Trained in the use of cleaning chemicals and equipment;
(d) Neatly uniformed with appropriate safety footwear and gloves.

2.4. The Contractor shall provide all cleaning materials, consumables, and equipment required for the Services, including but not limited to:
(a) Floor cleaning machines (scrubbers, polishers, vacuum cleaners);
(b) Cleaning chemicals, disinfectants, and detergents (environmentally friendly wherever feasible);
(c) Mops, brooms, wipers, dusters, and other cleaning tools;
(d) Garbage bags of appropriate sizes;
(e) Personal protective equipment for the deployed personnel.
